// Deployed to /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52unattended-upgrades-local on the VPS.
//
// A separate drop-in rather than edits to 50unattended-upgrades: that file is
// package-owned, and an upgrade of unattended-upgrades can prompt over or replace it.
// The 52 prefix sorts after 50, so these win.
//
// WHY: unattended-upgrades was already installing security updates, but with
// Automatic-Reboot unset nothing ever loaded them. On 2026-08-01 the box had been up 26
// weeks running kernel 6.8.0-90 while 6.8.0-136 and a newer libc6 sat installed and
// unused. Patched-but-not-running looks healthy from every angle except `uname -r`, which
// makes it a worse failure mode than being visibly unpatched.
//
// The tradeoff accepted: a single node with no HA means every reboot is a brief outage.
// A ~30s outage at a predictable hour beats an unbounded window of unloaded kernel fixes.

Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot "true";

// Reboot even when someone is logged in. Counter-intuitive, but on a headless box the
// only "user" is an admin SSH session — and a forgotten session would otherwise block
// reboots indefinitely, recreating exactly the problem this fixes.
Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot-WithUsers "true";

// UTC (the box runs Etc/UTC). 10:00 UTC is ~03:00 US Pacific / 06:00 Eastern — the
// quietest window for a North America-facing audience. Only fires when a reboot is
// actually required; it is not a nightly restart.
Unattended-Upgrade::Automatic-Reboot-Time "10:00";
